      "previewContent": "# RAU DEV </> — Session 01 Companion Lecture Notes\n\n## 1. Integer Overflow in CSES 1068 (Weird Algorithm)\nEven when n <= 10^6, intermediate values of 3n + 1 can exceed the 32-bit signed integer limit (2^31 - 1). In C++, always use `long long`.\n\n## 2. Extensible Code in Mock Interviews (Fizz Buzz)\nInstead of rigid chains of `elif`, store divisor rules in a list: `rules = [(3, 'Fizz'), (5, 'Buzz')]`. If an interviewer adds `7 -> 'Jazz'`, you only update the data table!\n\n## 3. Space-Time Tradeoffs (Intersection of Two Arrays)\n• Hash Set Approach: O(n + m) Time, O(min(n, m)) Space\n• Sorted Two-Pointer Approach: O(n log n + m log m) Time, O(1) Auxiliary Space"
