      "content": "What an incredible kickoff in **Room 515**! During our first Friday session (**01 // WELCOME**), we introduced the core departments behind RAU DEV—Executive, Tech, Logistics, and Tutoring—and established our four foundational principles: **Curiosity over ego**, **Progress over perfection**, **Collaboration over competition**, and **Respect at every level**.\n\n### Highlights from Session 01:\n- **The 30-Second Introduction:** Members paired up with someone new to share their name & year, their tech story, and one thing they'd love to learn or build.\n- **Starting Challenge:** We warmed up with **CSES 1068 (Weird Algorithm)**, exploring why 32-bit integers overflow on $3n+1$ and how to write clean solutions.\n- **Weekly & Optional Quests:** Members tackled **LeetCode 412 (Fizz Buzz)** and **LeetCode 349 (Intersection of Two Arrays)**, earning the very first XP points of the semester!\n- **Scoreboard Live:** Congratulations to **Andreea, Iulian Fecioru, Mihai, and Victor** for tying at the top of the Provisional Scoreboard with **35 XP** each, followed closely by **Luci (20 XP)** and **Denisa, Asik, Damian, and Cazacu (10 XP)**.\n\nAll slides and solution files from Session 01 are now available for download on the **Resources** page!"
